cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EEGTable in your research, please cite it as below, together with the
  methods and packages your analysis relied on, which each method page lists.
title: EEGTable
abstract: >-
  Labelled EEG feature extraction and modeling for MNE objects. Trial-level spectral,
  temporal, connectivity, complexity, cycle and microstate measures over named
  windows and baselines, whose columns carry units, computation parameters,
  coverage and provenance.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Duquette
    given-names: Joshua
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoshuaDuq/EEGTable"
url: "https://joshuaduq.github.io/EEGTable/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - EEG
  - MNE-Python
  - feature extraction
  - event-related desynchronization
  - provenance
